Noticed while doing k82, deliberately left alone because that ticket scoped
itself to one line and three agents were in the tree at the time.

lib/API/Docker/Role/Type.pm line 7:

  use Scalar::Util qw( blessed );

blessed is never called in the role. The only other occurrence of the word
is `convert_blessed => 1`, which is a hash key, not the function.

Since k82 the import no longer leaks onto the 201 generated classes, so
this costs nothing at runtime -- it is a dead import that tells the next
reader the role does something with references that it does not.

Check before removing whether anything reaches it through the role by
composition rather than by a direct call.

Done in 0978563, one deletion. The verification was the job and the agent did it by all three routes: no direct call and no fully-qualified one, the role is applied at exactly one site so the 201 generated classes are the whole consumer set and none answered ->blessed before or after, and every indirect dispatch in the role goes through a registry attribute name or a literal. Measured in a clean clone of HEAD rather than the shared tree, because k84 had staged deletions in the index at the time. No Changes entry, deliberately: since k82 the name was not exported to any class, so nothing a caller can observe moved.
